# A template call that leaves out an argument of the function it calls is refused by the
# checker, as a call is (Templates ch. 2), so the back end's guard "a template call that
# fills no argument at place j" (lower/templates.prism) is not reached. Written by Claude
# on the claude-lowering branch; subject to change.
Quote: fn Text, Text -> Text
fn Quote mark, text = "{mark} {text}"

Broken: fn Text -> Text
fn Broken t = inline_text <txt>
<@Quote text=<<t>>/>
</txt>
